Plan (short). Only these two files will be created.

1) src/auth/refresh.ts
- Imports: `createSession, getSession, revokeSession, type Session` from `./session.ts`
- Exports `refreshSession(token: string): Session | undefined`
- Looks up live session with `getSession(token)`, returns `undefined` if none
- Otherwise revokes it with `revokeSession(existing.token)` and returns `createSession(existing.userId)` (same pattern as login creating session from user.id)

Exact code:
```ts
import { createSession, getSession, revokeSession, type Session } from "./session.ts";

export function refreshSession(token: string): Session | undefined {
  const existing = getSession(token);
  if (!existing) return undefined;
  revokeSession(existing.token);
  return createSession(existing.userId);
}
```

2) test/refresh.test.ts (node:test, like test/session.test.ts)
- Imports: test, beforeEach from node:test, assert from node:assert/strict, createSession/getSession/resetSessions from ../src/auth/session.ts, refreshSession from ../src/auth/refresh.ts
- beforeEach calls resetSessions()
- Tests:
  - returns undefined if no live session exists
  - revokes old session and creates fresh session for same user (tokens differ, same userId, old token no longer live, new token live)

Exact code:
```ts
import { test, beforeEach } from "node:test";
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { createSession, getSession, resetSessions } from "../src/auth/session.ts";
import { refreshSession } from "../src/auth/refresh.ts";

beforeEach(() => resetSessions());

test("refreshSession returns undefined if no live session exists", () => {
  assert.equal(refreshSession("missing-token"), undefined);
});

test("refreshSession revokes old session and creates fresh session for same user", () => {
  const original = createSession("u_1");
  const refreshed = refreshSession(original.token);
  assert.ok(refreshed);
  assert.notEqual(refreshed.token, original.token);
  assert.equal(refreshed.userId, original.userId);
  assert.equal(getSession(original.token), undefined);
  assert.equal(getSession(refreshed.token)?.userId, "u_1");
});
```

